      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: EPS misses analyst expectations",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹15.76 (up from ₹13.11 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹36.1b (up 26% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹2.22b (up 20% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 6.1% (down from 6.4% in 3Q 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 5.2%. Revenue is forecast to grow 13% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 11% growth forecast for the Auto Components industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 23% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 22% per year.",
